# General Rules

## Before Making Changes
- Read docs/PRD.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, docs/DESIGN.md
- Understand what already exists — do NOT duplicate logic
- Make a plan for any change larger than 20 lines
- Never modify unrelated files

## Code Quality
- Use TypeScript — no `any` types without justification
- Keep functions focused and small
- Reuse existing components and utilities
- Prefer editing over rewriting

## File Structure
- Frontend: App.tsx (single file by design — do not split without explicit instruction)
- Backend: server.js + api/*.js
- Documentation: docs/

## After Changes
- Run `npx tsc --noEmit` — must pass
- Run `npm run build:web` — must succeed
- Update TASKS.md and docs/MEMORY.md

## Git
- Small, focused commits
- Format: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`
- Never commit .env files
